From 00ae5ba4daef8f5034df3d7fcd641226375e5281 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:05:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dsv41): normalize 1-row Engram column-slice stride when
 24 % tp != 0

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head e3ab3f3da27ccb4b5deb5a919982d87e962704ab.

Rationale:
When 24 % tp_size != 0 (TP=5 with 5 columns/rank -> 6,400 gathered width, or TP=7 with 4 columns/rank -> 7,168 gathered width), interleaved_rows and interleaved_sp_rows slice rows[:, : 24 * 256].contiguous(), and EngramColumnParallelLinear.forward slices output[..., : self.logical_output_size].contiguous(). For a single-row batch (tokens == 1 during warmup and 1-row CUDA graph capture), PyTorch treats a (1, 6144) slice with stride (6400, 1) or (7168, 1) as already contiguous (shape[0] == 1), so .contiguous() returns the slice unchanged with stride(0) == 6400 or 7168. per_token_cast_impl then requests get_per_token_cast_kernel_cuda(hidden=6144, token_stride=6400), raising KernelNotPreparedError against the frozen kernel cache (which prepares token_stride=6144). Chaining .view(..., 24 * 256) (and .view(*output.shape[:-1], self.logical_output_size)) normalizes stride(0) to the logical width when tokens == 1, while remaining unreachable on TP=1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8 where 24 % tp_size == 0.

Quality:
Bit-identical on all divisor TP shapes (TP=1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8: early return before slice); restores packed row stride on TP=5 and TP=7 for 1-row steps.

Tests:
- pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_engram.py -k test_interleaved_rows_restore_column_order (16 passed across tp_size in 1..8 and tokens in {1, 5}).

Upstream status: local fix for 0750 column-interleaved disk Engram on non-divisor TP sizes.
